From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pyroshine Vendor Maintenance <vendor@pyroshine.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:18:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] encoder: allocate DPB images at the input-image width

NVIDIA's encoder (RTX 3080, driver 615.78) writes reconstructed 8-bit
2-plane 4:4:4 chroma with the pitch it derives from the 64-aligned luma
pitch, the same defect patch 0001 avoids for input images. DPB images were
still created at the coded width, so at widths with width % 64 in 1..=32
the chroma writes overran the image: reference pictures were corrupted
(decoded chroma errors of ~200 codes growing over P frames at 1440x768
H.264 4:4:4) and, when the overrun reached unmapped memory, NVENC faulted
(Xid 31, FAULT_PTE ACCESS_TYPE_VIRT_WRITE) and the device was lost.

Create DPB images with the input-image width. Pictures keep the coded
extent through each picture resource's codedExtent.
---
 src/encoder/codec.rs | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/encoder/codec.rs b/src/encoder/codec.rs
index fe0a696..a73b56c 100644
--- a/src/encoder/codec.rs
+++ b/src/encoder/codec.rs
@@ -545,6 +545,13 @@ pub(crate) fn query_video_caps(
 /// The two differ when `width % 64` is 1..=32 (e.g. 1360, 1440, 2400), and the
 /// decoded chroma comes out sheared. With a 64-aligned image width they are
 /// always equal; other formats and implementations ignore the extra columns.
+///
+/// The encoder writes reconstructed pictures into the DPB with the same pitch,
+/// so DPB images use this width as well. At a coded width the chroma writes
+/// overran the image: references were corrupted (decoded chroma errors of
+/// ~200 codes growing over P frames at 1440x768 H.264 4:4:4) and, when the
+/// overrun reached unmapped memory, NVENC faulted (Xid 31, `VIRT_WRITE`) and
+/// the device was lost.
 pub(crate) fn input_image_width(coded_width: u32, max_coded_width: u32) -> u32 {
     const INPUT_IMAGE_WIDTH_ALIGNMENT: u32 = 64;
     coded_width
@@ -694,9 +701,12 @@ pub(crate) fn build_encoder_common(req: &CommonInitRequest) -> Result<CommonInit
         tracing::info!("Using layered DPB (driver does not support separate reference images)");
     }
 
+    // DPB images use the input-image width too: NVIDIA writes reconstructed
+    // 8-bit 4:4:4 chroma with the same mis-computed pitch (see
+    // `input_image_width`), past the end of a coded-width image.
     let (dpb_images, dpb_image_memories, dpb_image_views) = create_dpb_images(
         context,
-        aligned_width,
+        input_image_extent.width,
         aligned_height,
         reference_picture_format,
         dpb_slot_count,
